{
  "summary": "The bug stems from the server's unconditional replacement of client features on every state_update message (hub.go:354). Three TUI code paths call FeatureFile.list_all() without a board filter and push results to the server: the periodic push (tui.py:2093, every 5 seconds), the auto-refresh handler (tui.py:2636), and the auto-mode toggle (tui.py:2137). If list_all() returns an empty list — due to a transient filesystem issue, timing during startup before boards are initialized, or a brief I/O glitch — the server replaces the entire feature list with nothing. The webui then polls /api/board, gets the empty state from the server, and renders zero items. Potential fixes include: (1) adding a guard in hub.go to reject empty feature lists when the previous state was non-empty (stale-is-better-than-empty pattern), (2) having the TUI validate that list_all() returned a non-empty result before pushing (or at least log a warning), and (3) adding a timestamp or sequence number to state_update messages so the server can detect stale or out-of-order updates. The simplest immediate fix is option 1 — refuse to overwrite a non-empty feature list with an empty one on the server side."
}
